<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλῆ</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλοῦς</span>) a marg. mark used by Gramm.
		(&lt;*&gt;, &lt;*&gt;), to indicate vv. <i><span class="en">
			Il.
		</span></i>, rejected verses, etc., and, in dramatic poetry, a new speaker,
			<i><span class="en">
			Cic.
			<u>Att.</u>
			8.2.4
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Heph.
		</span></i>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Poëm.</i><i><span class="en">
				p.74C.
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1086 ii 55
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a dance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.105
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλαῖ, αἱ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίπλωμα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1054
			</span></i><i>b:</i> also sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				5.446
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διπλοΐς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ap.Ty.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
